<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zonians</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zonians were the American civilians who lived and worked in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal-zone">Panama Canal Zone</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> administration from 1904 to 1979. Many were employees of the canal company and their families, living in subsidised company towns with their own schools, shops and police. Their privileged and segregated enclave was resented by Panamanians, and most left after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/torrijos-carter-treaties">Torrijos–Carter Treaties</a> ended the zone.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zonians.jpg" alt="Zonians" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BMacZero · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Panama_Canal_Zone.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
